@Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress = http://localhost:5219

### --- DATABASE HEALTH CHECKS ---

### 1. Check BOTH Redis & PostgreSQL Health
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/database/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Check Redis Health
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/database/redis
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Check PostgreSQL Health
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/database/postgres
Accept: application/json

###


### --- SITE BANNER (REDIS STRINGS) ---

### 4. Set Site Banner in Redis
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/site-banner/set-banner
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "banner": "Welcome to Chai aur Redis! Enjoy 50% discount!"
}

###

### 5. Check if Site Banner Exists in Redis
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/site-banner/banner/exists
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Get Site Banner from Redis
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/site-banner/get-banner
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Delete Site Banner from Redis
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/site-banner/delete-banner
Accept: application/json

###


### --- OTP FLOW (REDIS TTL) ---

### 8. Generate OTP (30s TTL)
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/otp/generate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "9876543210"
}

###

### 9. Check OTP Remaining TTL
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/otp/9876543210/ttl
Accept: application/json

###

### 10. Verify OTP
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phoneNumber": "9876543210",
  "otp": "123456"
}

###

### 11. Delete OTP
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/otp/9876543210
Accept: application/json

###


### --- USER JSON & HASH (REDIS OBJECT STORAGE) ---

### 12. Save User as JSON (Redis String)
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hitesh Choudhary",
  "email": "hitesh@example.com",
  "role": "Teacher",
  "channel": "Chai aur Code"
}

###

### 13. Get User JSON
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/json
Accept: application/json

###

### 14. Save User as Hash (Redis Hash)
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/hash
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Hitesh Choudhary",
  "email": "hitesh@example.com",
  "role": "Instructor",
  "location": "Jaipur"
}

###

### 15. Get Entire User Hash (HGETALL)
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/hash
Accept: application/json

###

### 16. Get Specific Field from User Hash (HGET)
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/hash/email
Accept: application/json

###

### 17. Delete User JSON Only
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/json
Accept: application/json

###

### 18. Delete User Hash Only
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101/hash
Accept: application/json

###

### 19. Delete Both JSON and Hash for User
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/user/101
Accept: application/json

###


### --- EMAIL QUEUE (REDIS LISTS - FIFO) ---

### 20. Push Email to Queue (LPUSH)
POST {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/emails
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "to": "student@example.com",
  "subject": "Welcome to Chai aur Redis!",
  "body": "Here is your course confirmation."
}

###

### 21. Check Queue Length (LLEN)
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/emails/length
Accept: application/json

###

### 22. Peek Pending Queue Items (LRANGE)
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/emails/peek?count=5
Accept: application/json

###

### 23. Pop & Process One Email (RPOP)
GET {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/emails/process-one
Accept: application/json

###

### 24. Clear Email Queue (DEL)
DELETE {{Chai_aur_Redis_HostAddress}}/api/emails
Accept: application/json

###
